{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:NuclearInteractions.SpinFromSo3Fiber","@type":"LeanModule","name":"NuclearInteractions.SpinFromSo3Fiber","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.spinFromSo3Fiber_refutable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.spinFromSo3Fiber_refutable","kind":"theorem","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/spin-from-so3-fiber.lean#L137-L147","doc":"The class is **refutable**, which the previous `holds : Prop` carrier was not: the\nconstant-zero map satisfies `h_squared_vanishes` and fails `h_fourth_eq`.\n\nStated as a theorem rather than left to the docstring because \"the carrier asserts\nsomething\" is precisely the property that was missing, and a reader should see it\ndischarged rather than take the prose's word. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.SpinFromSo3Fiber.h_fourth_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.SpinFromSo3Fiber.h_fourth_eq","kind":"theorem","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/spin-from-so3-fiber.lean#L135-L135","doc":"The **first non-trivial** coefficient is `h⁴ = −3/4`, supplied by `ℓ = 2`. This is the\nload-bearing `h⁴` closure gap the block names. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.SpinFromSo3Fiber.h_squared_vanishes","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.SpinFromSo3Fiber.h_squared_vanishes","kind":"theorem","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/spin-from-so3-fiber.lean#L132-L132","doc":"The Borromean Markov trace's exact closed form has **`h² = 0`** — the `ℓ = 1` level\ncontributes nothing, which is why the `S₃`-truncated Family A weight (ending at `h²`)\ncannot see the structure. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.SpinFromSo3Fiber.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.SpinFromSo3Fiber.mk","kind":"ctor","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/spin-from-so3-fiber.lean#L128-L128","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.SpinFromSo3Fiber","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.SpinFromSo3Fiber","kind":"class","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/spin-from-so3-fiber.lean#L116-L135","doc":"**CONJECTURE (D10).** Spin `SU(2)_S` as the continuous `SO(3)` lift on the three colour\nsheets, via the `S₅ → A₅ ≅ I ⊂ SO(3)` icosahedral embedding on Bring's quintic.\n\n`levelCoeff` is the block's own named missing object — the map from spherical-harmonic\nlevel to the Wedderburn coefficient it contributes to the 3-strand `H₃` trace, with\n`levelCoeff n` the coefficient of `h^(2n)`. It is supplied by the **caller**, so the class\nis false for maps that do not take the block's values (see the refutability theorem below).\n\n**No instance is provided.** Downstream results consume this as `[SpinFromSo3Fiber f]` and\nare genuinely conditional on it.\n\n-- Ref: [leitner2026] conj:spin-from-so3-fiber ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:spin-from-so3-fiber","label":"conj:spin-from-so3-fiber","md":"quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/spin-from-so3-fiber.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.familyA_linking_weight_closed_form","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.familyA_linking_weight_closed_form","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/spin-from-so3-fiber.lean#L103-L114","doc":"**The Family A linking weight, in closed form.** The block states\n`(3q² + 4 + 3q⁻²)/4 = 5/2 + (3/4)h²` with `h = q - q⁻¹`, and that it *terminates* at `h²`.\n\nThis is an identity, not a conjecture, so it is a **theorem** rather than a class field —\nthe part of the block that can be discharged is discharged. It is what makes \"Family A\nterminates at `h²`\" a statement about the truncation rather than about the algebra. ","signatureChunk":0}]}